  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Two positive numbers differ by 7 and the sum of their squares is 169. Find the numbers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$5$ and $12$.",
      "worked": "Let the smaller number be $x$, so the larger number is $x+7$ and $x>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+(x+7)^2&=169\\\\2x^2+14x+49&=169\\\\2x^2+14x-120&=0\\\\x^2+7x-60&=0\\\\(x+12)(x-5)&=0\\\\x&=-12\\text{ or }x=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nReject $x=-12$ because the numbers are positive. The larger number is $5+7=12$.\n\nThe numbers are $5$ and $12$. Check: $12-5=7$ and $5^2+12^2=25+144=169$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 85
  },
